WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.155
Six projects.

2
00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:04.629
A crew already moving.

3
00:00:04.795 --> 00:00:07.523
Let's give Docket a new superpower: smart

4
00:00:07.523 --> 00:00:10.170
summaries, written onto its knowledge graph every

5
00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:10.655
night.

6
00:00:11.203 --> 00:00:14.129
Tell Firstmate the goal: summarize changed nodes

7
00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:17.423
overnight, keep the evidence, and show what's new.

8
00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:18.901
The task appears on deck.

9
00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.140
A worker picks it up.

10
00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:21.661
Open the task.

11
00:00:21.919 --> 00:00:24.508
There's the brief, live progress, conversation,

12
00:00:24.508 --> 00:00:25.458
and checks.

13
00:00:26.238 --> 00:00:28.421
Jump into Changes to see exactly what the

14
00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:29.475
worker is building.

15
00:00:29.791 --> 00:00:33.041
A decision lands in chat: summarize everything, or

16
00:00:33.041 --> 00:00:34.304
only changed nodes?

17
00:00:34.957 --> 00:00:36.893
Choose changed nodes.

18
00:00:37.674 --> 00:00:39.726
Lower cost, fresher knowledge.

19
00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:41.282
Tap Decide.

20
00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:42.280
Back to work.

21
00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:45.531
Here's the result, running inside Wheelhouse.

22
00:00:45.696 --> 00:00:48.724
Open a node: a fresh summary, linked evidence,

23
00:00:48.796 --> 00:00:50.047
and last night's run.

24
00:00:50.248 --> 00:00:52.535
Share for review, or send focused feedback

25
00:00:52.535 --> 00:00:53.681
straight to Firstmate.

26
00:00:53.998 --> 00:00:55.771
Read the report in the reading view.

27
00:00:55.971 --> 00:00:58.871
Inspect the pull request, change by change.

28
00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:00.322
Approve the merge.

29
00:01:00.453 --> 00:01:01.042
Landed.

30
00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:05.048
Meanwhile, Atlas is testing, Compass is building,

31
00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:06.812
and Beacon needs a call.

32
00:01:07.187 --> 00:01:09.216
Harbour brings every project together.

33
00:01:09.532 --> 00:01:11.050
Radar shows the flow.

34
00:01:11.366 --> 00:01:14.396
The bell, decisions, time, and headroom tell you

35
00:01:14.396 --> 00:01:15.438
where to look next.

36
00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:18.109
Second mates bring more crews aboard.

37
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:21.234
Plugins add reviews, project links, issues, and

38
00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.195
team knowledge.

39
00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:25.147
The Vault grants secrets by name, while their

40
00:01:25.147 --> 00:01:26.700
values stay in the keychain.

41
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.803
Remotes and Wheelhouse Cloud bring your own

42
00:01:29.803 --> 00:01:31.297
machine to another browser.

43
00:01:31.614 --> 00:01:33.529
On your phone, the same bridge goes with

44
00:01:33.529 --> 00:01:33.910
you.

45
00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.802
The setup wizard gets you aboard.

46
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:37.532
Updates keep you current.

47
00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:40.298
One idea, a whole crew, and a clear

48
00:01:40.298 --> 00:01:41.259
path to shipped.

49
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:42.722
That's Wheelhouse.
